<title>USA: Borg-Warner on course for EPS growth.</title>
<headline>Borg-Warner on course for EPS growth.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Borg-Warner Security Corp said Tuesday it was on course for achieving its previously stated 1997 earnings per share growth target of 30 to 45 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;First quarter results reflect our continued progress,&quot; chairman Joe Adorjan said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company reported first-quarter earnings of $0.17 per share compared to $0.02 a year ago, which included a $0.05 per share loss from discontinued operations.</p>
<p>	  ((Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
